<title>USA: Life Re reinsures $102mln of UNUM policies.</title>
<headline>Life Re reinsures $102mln of UNUM policies.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Life Re Corp said Thursday its subsidiary Life Reassurance Corp of America agreed to reinsure $102 million of UNUM Corp's UNUM Life Insurance Co of America insurance policies.</p>
<p>Life Re said Life Reassurance will co-insure and administer the 16,000 individual stock life insurance and annuity contracts with statutory policy reserves of $102 million as of June 30.  </p>
<p>Life Re said disability insurer UNUM of Portland, Maine, stopped selling the policies in the 1980s.</p>
<p>The company added the reinsurance agreement became effective July 1.</p>
</text>
